From: port_ios lavender
Subject: [PATCH 0213] lavender: CDC-NCM USB function for Windows, bus reset handling

With 0210-0212 the phone enumerates on Windows at high speed (log
sweetlog-usbtest-0212: address 99, all descriptors) as "Sweet iOS (USB
Ethernet)" VID 1209 PID 0001, class 02/06 (CDC-ECM), problem code 28:
Windows has no ECM driver. Windows 10 2004+/11 ships UsbNcm for CDC-NCM.

- sweetusbncm=1 (default on LAVENDER; 0 keeps CDC-ECM for macOS/Linux):
  NCM descriptors (comm 02/0D/00 + NCM functional, data 0A/00/01), class
  requests GET_NTB_PARAMETERS (NTB16, 2 KiB both ways, divisor and
  alignment 4), GET/SET_NTB_FORMAT, GET/SET_NTB_INPUT_SIZE, packet filter;
  OUT NTB16 parsing (chained NDP16 tables, several datagrams, bounds
  checked, bad blocks counted); IN frames in an NTH16 + one NDP16
  (datagram at 28; a 512-byte block gets one pad byte).
- CONNECTION_SPEED_CHANGE (NCM: speed then connection, as Linux f_ncm;
  ECM: connection then speed, as f_ecm / bergamota 0108).
- Bus reset / disconnect (bergamota 0107, Linux dwc3 gadget reset): end
  outstanding transfers, clear stalls, drop the data endpoints and the
  configuration, ep0 back to SETUP; Windows resets the device several
  times while it binds a driver.

